<title>PERU: Peru's October copper output rises 15.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru's October copper output rises 15.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's copper output rose 15.7 percent to 44,943 tonnes in October compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Monday.</p>
<p>Production rose 20.01 percent to 400,306 tonnes in the first ten months of the year compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>In 1995, copper output rose 10.8 percent to 404,990 tonnes from 365,513 tonnes in 1994.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's sixth largest copper producer. The country's largest producer, Southern Peru Copper Corp, accounts for around 60 percent of the country's output.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
